 "result": "csvsum.py is a single-pass Python reader: it reads stdin as bytes, splits on newlines, skips the header, splits each line on commas, sums the val column per cat in a dict, then writes cats sorted with '%.2f' formatting. It passes the sample check (output matched out-0.txt) and is registered at baseline 2.04016. The one variant I tried (dropping the per-line rstrip) scored 2.06 against an incumbent of 2.057, so it was not adopted. Further gains look marginal, so I am stopping here to conserve energy.",
